# Pairs with UniqueOwner. LiftFenceUnlessSwappedAsync loses its registry check
# and lifts the old copy's fence after a flip that did land, so T serves again
# while the alias names R.
MODULE: UniqueOwnerLiftAfterLandedFlip
TARGET: UniqueOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the fence is lifted after a flip that landed, so the old copy serves beside the new one
PERTURBS: ResizeFlipRefused

--- FIND
ResizeFlipRefused ==
    /\ rz = "copied"
    /\ fence # {}
    /\ refusals > 0
    /\ alias = T
--- REPLACE
ResizeFlipRefused ==
\* MUTATION: the lift ignores whether the alias moved.
    /\ rz \in {"copied", "swapped"}
    /\ fence # {}
    /\ refusals > 0
--- END